 ¿Se puede subir el recall de malnutrición ajustando el propio KNN? Probamos k y weights.\n","filas = []\n","for w in ['uniform', 'distance']:\n","    for k in [5, 11, 15, 21, 31]:\n","        knn = KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=k, weights=w).fit(X_train, y_train)\n","        yp = knn.predict(X_test)\n","        filas.append({'weights': w, 'k': k,\n","                      'recall_malnut': round(recall_score(y_test, yp), 3),\n","                      'accuracy': round(knn.score(X_test, y_test), 3)})\n","pd.DataFrame(filas)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"HVnk1EDWBQxP"},"source":["Ajustar `k` y `weights` **no resuelve** el problema: el recall de malnutrición se mantiene bajo (~0,07–0,25) e incluso **empeora** al aumentar `k`, porque con más vecinos el modelo se apoya todavía más en la clase mayoritaria. La accuracy sube un poco, pero a costa de detectar aún menos casos de riesgo. La mejor configuración para el recall es `weights='distance'` con `k=5`."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":114,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":213,"status":"ok","timestamp":1782062335931,"user":{"displayName":"Franco Nicolai Corvalán Mansourova","userId":"03669814590806608851"},"user_tz":240},"id":"iA5xa9LDBTJE","outputId":"671fbc48-a438-4926-be41-1b6b49d44ab7"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Matriz de confusión [normal, malnutrición]:\n","[[288  54]\n"," [ 92  30]]\n","              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n","\n","      normal       0.76      0.84      0.80       342\n","malnutrición       0.36      0.25      0.29       122\n","\n","    accuracy                           0.69       464\n","   macro avg       0.56      0.54      0.54       464\n","weighted avg       0.65      0.69      0.66       464\n","\n"]}],"source":["# Mejor configuración para el recall de malnutrición: weights='distance', k=5\n","knn = KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=5, weights='distance').fit(X_train, y_train)\n","y_pred = knn.predict(X_test)\n","print('Matriz de confusión [normal, malnutrición]:')\n","print(confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred))\n","print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred, target_names=['normal', 'malnutrición'], zero_division=0))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"CFjSyDXwBU6Z"},"source":["**no se logra subir el recall de malnutrición**: ni ajustando el número de vecinos `k` ni la ponderación `weights`. Al contrario, al aumentar `k` el recall **baja**, porque el modelo se apoya cada vez más en la clase mayoritaria por el desbalance (~74/26). La mejor configuración (`distance`, `k=5`) detecta apenas ~1 de cada 4 niños con malnutrición, en línea con el baseline.\n","\n","Es un **resultado normal**: el KNN, queda limitado por el desbalance para detectar la clase minoritaria. Mejorar sustancialmente este recall no es posible en base a los contenidos del curso. Por lo que a futuro, podriamos usar técnicas como reponderación de clases, ajuste de umbral o modelos específicos para datos desbalanceados.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"3FCXu21_7wh3"},"source":["# Clustering"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"KH0kq89uad79"},"source":["Objetivo 2 del proyecto: *categorizar perfiles de niños en seguimiento*.\n","\n","> **encoding + MinMaxScaler → PCA(0.95) → AgglomerativeClustering / GMM →\n","> selección con Silhouette (HAC) y AIC (GMM) → caracterización de perfiles.**\n","\n","Se agrupa a los niños por su **perfil intrahospitalario** (sin usar el seguimiento) y luego\n","se describe cada grupo."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":115,"metadata":{"executionInfo":{"elapsed":6,"status":"ok","timestamp":1782062335941,"user":{"displayName":"Franco Nicolai Corvalán Mansourova","userId":"03669814590806608851"},"user_tz":240},"id":"rcoEpycDaZBF"},"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.cluster import AgglomerativeClustering\n","from sklearn.mixture import GaussianMixture\n","from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n","from scipy.cluster.hierarchy import dendrogram"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"JrXqUvlVhQzt"},"source":["## Matriz de perfil intrahospitalario\n","\n","Se aplica PCA(0.95)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":116,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":196,"status":"ok","timestamp":1782062336142,"user":{"displayName":"Franco Nicolai Corvalán Mansourova","userId":"03669814590806608851"},"user_tz":240},"id":"HLRXemJ2anCS","outputId":"d310dbda-7d7f-459d-8ae9-b38cc5675153"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Features: (3327, 45) -> PCA(0.95): (3327, 16)\n"]}],"source":["dfc = df.copy()\n","dfc['Tuvo_sepsis'] = (dfc['Sepsis tardía - germen primer evento'] != 220).astype(int)\n","dfc['Severidad DBP'] = dfc['Severidad DBP'].astype('Int64').astype(str)\n","dfc['Tipo de parto'] = dfc['Tipo de parto'].astype('Int64').astype(str).replace('<NA>', 'NA')\n","dfc['Fenton al nacer'] = dfc['Fenton al nacer'].fillna('NA').astype(str)\n","dfc['Talla al alta'] = dfc['Talla al alta'].where(dfc['Talla al alta'].between(25, 80))\n","dfc['CC al alta']    = dfc['CC al alta'].where(dfc['CC al alta'].between(18, 45))\n","dfc['Peso al alta']  = dfc['Peso al alta'].where(dfc['Peso al alta'].between(400, 7000))\n","\n","num_c = ['Peso al nacer', 'EG al nacer', 'Edad de la madre', 'Score Neocosur',\n","         'Días de VM', 'Duración oxígeno días', 'EG_Alta', 'Peso al alta',\n","         'Talla al alta', 'CC al alta', 'Días de estadía']\n","cat_c = ['Sexo', 'Multiple', 'Corticoides prenatales', 'Malformación congénita mayor',\n","         'Hemorragia Intraventricular (HIV)', 'Leucomalacia', 'Hidrocefalia', 'ECN',\n","         'Recibe Surfactante', 'O2 36 semanas', 'Tuvo_sepsis', 'Severidad DBP',\n","         'Tipo de parto', 'Fenton al nacer']\n","\n","Xc = pd.concat([dfc[num_c].apply(lambda s: s.fillna(s.median())),\n","                pd.get_dummies(dfc[cat_c].astype(str), drop_first=False)], axis=1).astype(float)\n","Xc = preprocessing.MinMaxScaler().fit_transform(Xc)\n","Xpc = PCA(n_components=0.95).fit_transform(Xc)\n","print('Features:', Xc.shape, '-> PCA(0.95):', Xpc.shape)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Ed3yt3t5aqrm"},"source":["Agrupamos a los niños por sus variables\n","**intrahospitalarias** (no usamos el seguimiento). Tras one-hot + escalado y PCA al 95 %, el espacio\n","queda en **16 componentes**, sobre el cual aplicamos el clustering."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"K4MmZ4zDavRm"},"source":["## HAC\n","\n","Silhouette por linkage y por nº de clusters"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":117,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":4612,"status":"ok","timestamp":1782062340747,"user":{"displayName":"Franco Nicolai Corvalán Mansourova","userId":"03669814590806608851"},"user_tz":240},"id":"cUix8b6gavA8","outputId":"784b7697-b8cb-4a67-d50a-6d89bdce1c57"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Silhouette por linkage (k=3):\n","  single   : 0.204\n","  average  : 0.218\n","  complete : 0.200\n","  ward     : 0.081\n","\n","Silhouette ward por nº de clusters:\n","  k=2: 0.227\n","  k=3: 0.081\n","  k=4: 0.099\n","  k=5: 0.087\n","  k=6: 0.093\n","  k=7: 0.101\n","-> Mejor k (ward): 2 (silhouette=0.227)\n"]}],"source":["print('Silhouette por linkage (k=3):')\n","for link in ['single', 'average', 'complete', 'ward']:\n","    lab = AgglomerativeClustering(linkage=link, n_clusters=3).fit(Xpc).labels_\n","    print(f'  {link:9s}: {silhouette_score(Xpc, lab):.3f}')\n","\n","print('\\nSilhouette ward por nº de clusters:')\n","best_k, best_s = 2, -1\n","for k in range(2, 8):\n","    lab = AgglomerativeClustering(linkage='ward', n_clusters=k).fit(Xpc).labels_\n","    s = silhouette_score(Xpc, lab)\n","    print(f'  k={k}: {s:.3f}')\n","    if s > best_s: best_k, best_s = k, s\n","print(f'-> Mejor k (ward): {best_k} (silhouette={best_s:.3f})')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ZefcHQjOaz0e"},"source":["El **Silhouette** mide qué tan bien separados están los\n","grupos (más alto = mejor). Entre los *linkages*, los mejores rondan 0,20–0,22. Al variar el número\n","de clusters con *ward*, el mejor valor se da en **k = 2 (Silhouette ≈ 0,23)**. Son valores **bajos**,\n","lo que es esperable en datos clínicos reales: no hay grupos perfectamente separados, pero **k = 2**\n","entrega la partición más limpia e interpretable."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"aLLLxTWea2VK"},"source":["### Dendrograma"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":118,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":424},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":623,"status":"ok","timestamp":1782062341373,"user":{"displayName":"Franco Nicolai Corvalán Mansourova","userId":"03669814590806608851"},"user_tz":240},"id":"CZPtAmi-aqHQ","outputId":"cef4d628-2809-4b73-d01d-19d843dcc696"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x400 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["def plot_dendrogram(model, **kwargs):\n","    counts = np.zeros(model.children_.shape[0])\n","    n = len(model.labels_)\n","    for i, merge in enumerate(model.children_):\n","        c = 0\n","        for idx in merge:\n","            c += 1 if idx < n else counts[idx - n]\n","        counts[i] = c\n","    Z = np.column_stack([model.children_, model.distances_, counts]).astype(float)\n","    dendrogram(Z, **kwargs)\n","\n","hac_full = AgglomerativeClustering(distance_threshold=0, linkage='ward', n_clusters=None).fit(Xpc)\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 4))\n","plt.title('Dendrograma (ward)')\n","plot_dendrogram(hac_full, truncate_mode='level', p=4)\n","plt.xlabel('Pacientes (o grupos)'); plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"DCGWv7HVa7IB"},"source":["Muestra cómo se van fusionando los pacientes/grupos según su\n","similitud; la altura de cada unión indica la distancia a la que se juntan. Un corte alto deja pocos\n","grupos grandes. Es coherente con la elección de **2 perfiles** principales."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"J46I5bqta9ku"},"source":["## GMM\n","\n","Se utiliza la curva AIC para elegir nº de componentes"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":119,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":489},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":7638,"status":"ok","timestamp":1782062349017,"user":{"displayName":"Franco Nicolai Corvalán Mansourova","userId":"03669814590806608851"},"user_tz":240},"id":"OzTNH7Dua4du","outputId":"d2b2b485-eecf-46e0-977d-e87d480f796a"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["n con menor AIC: 10\n"]}],"source":["ns = np.arange(1, 11)\n","aics = [GaussianMixture(n, covariance_type='full', random_state=RNG).fit(Xpc).aic(Xpc) for n in ns]\n","plt.plot(ns, aics, marker='o'); plt.xlabel('n_components'); plt.ylabel('AIC')\n","plt.title('GMM — AIC'); plt.grid(True); plt.show()\n","print('n con menor AIC:', ns[int(np.argmin(aics))])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"42GihtAObC0q"},"source":["El criterio **AIC** del GMM sigue bajando al aumentar el número de\n","componentes, nos quedamos con la partición de **HAC en 2\n","perfiles** para caracterizar los grupos."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"WawFiRoUbEx6"},"source":["## Caracterización de los perfiles"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":120,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":317},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":595,"status":"ok","timestamp":1782062349603,"user":{"displayName":"Franco Nicolai Corvalán Mansourova","userId":"03669814590806608851"},"user_tz":240},"id":"KNuvPqlrbAqo","outputId":"e024246c-6254-477e-c79a-23aec1b13f44"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Tamaño por perfil:\n","cluster\n","0    2817\n","1     510\n","\n","Medias por perfil:\n"]},{"out